  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa MPox Outbreak 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024, 13 African countries have reported a total of 3,591 cases and 23&#xa0;&#xa0;deaths from Monkeypox virus (MPXV), with an average Case Fatality Ratio (CFR) of 0.6% - which is at the lower end of reported variation in MPXV CFR, of 0% - 11%). Of these, nine continue to have active MPXV transmission in July/ August 2024: Burundi, Cameroon, CAR, Congo, C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, DRC, Kenya, Liberia, Nigeria, Rwanda, South Africa, and Uganda (WHO data as of 28th August 2024).
&#xa0;
IFRC has launched an emergency appeal seeking 30 million Swiss francs to support 40 million people in 12 countries initially and categorised as a red emergency. These include High risk: DRC; Moderate Risk: Cameroon, Burundi, Rwanda, Uganda, Nigeria, Cote d&#x2019;Ivoire, Central African Republic, South Africa, Kenya, Congo Brazzaville and Liberia.</narrative>
  </description>
